# Allowlist for scripts/ci/no-private-refs.sh — a security decision, not a convenience.
#
# One rule per line, `path/glob:pattern  # justification`. The glob matches the repo-relative
# path; the pattern is an ERE matched against the whole `git grep` hit (`path:line:text`).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. A justification is mandatory in review.
#
# ⛔ Do NOT add an entry to keep a real internal hostname, address or private repository path
# in a public tree. Remove it instead. An entry is only for a string that *looks* private but
# is not: a documented loopback example, a placeholder, or a term that collides with a rule.
#
# The guard and this file necessarily spell the patterns out; the guard excludes both from
# its own scan. Everything else is scanned.
#
# No entries by default. An empty file that fails the build is the correct starting state.

# Phase 3B (2026-11-14). The executor's security code and its oracle fixtures necessarily spell
# out the hostnames and addresses they REFUSE — a deny list is the mechanism, so those literals
# are the test, not a description of this estate. None of these names resolves to our
# infrastructure: `licences.internal`/`auth.internal` are URL-validation placeholders in unit
# tests, and the fixture addresses are the IANA shared (100.64/10) and metadata
# (100.100.100.200) ranges used as "must be blocked" cases. The suffix strings (`.internal`,
# `x.svc.cluster.local`) are the reference's own tenant deny list.
src/config.rs:(licences|auth)\.internal
src/worker/sources.rs:"\.internal",
src/worker/broker/egress.rs:"\.internal",
tests/fixtures/phase3b/generate_policy.py:(100\.64\.0\.1|100\.100\.100\.200|db\.internal|x\.svc\.cluster\.local)
tests/fixtures/phase3b/policy.json:(100\.64\.0\.1|100\.100\.100\.200|db\.internal|x\.svc\.cluster\.local)
